            "title": "You’ve Tried Different Bottles, but Feeding Still Feels Exhausting",
            "body": "<p>You’ve changed nipple flows, switched formulas, stopped mid-feed to burp, and bought bottles that all promised calmer feeding. Yet your baby may still click, gulp, pull away, or become uncomfortable afterward.</p><p>Meanwhile, your cupboard keeps filling with bottles you no longer use.</p><p>Parents often assume they just haven’t found the right brand yet. But sometimes the real problem is the bottle itself—how it controls airflow, what materials touch the milk, and how many frustrating pieces it adds to your routine.</p>"
          }
        },
